  "limitations": [
    "Evaluation uses synthetic telemetry, not production incidents.",
    "Fault onset is defined by simulator thresholds.",
    "A horizon-valid hit requires a matching predicted fault type and onset strictly after prediction time but no later than predictedWindowMinutes.",
    "Correctly classified warnings outside the returned horizon are reported separately and are not counted as horizon-valid hits.",
    "Early-warning episode metrics count an episode once if it has at least one matching-type out-of-horizon warning; overlapping windows are not independent.",
    "Active-rule detections are tracked separately from future forecasts.",
    "A stable recovery window requires all 15 input readings to be labeled normal.",
    "Five episodes per class are only a smoke evaluation, not a reliability estimate."
  ]
